e  he says the five-day course used to be  reserved for high-risk assignments  now it's standard for anyone going help  each other out  these skills will serve you if it's a  natural disaster someplace or an  incident of crime  a medical emergency i think it just  makes our diplomats better prepared no  matter where they go  this smokehouse simulation teaches them  how to escape a dark burning building  and was added as a direct result of what  happened in libya  trainees also undergo hours of precision  driving  which in my case was  somewhat less than precise did you miss  it i think you might have missed it i  don't know i think i killed it  the final exam is every diplomat's worst  nightmare  an embassy siege the goal is to make it  as realistic as possible so we've got an  embassy that's on fire behind us and  then as they're trying to evacuate  they come across a building full of  casualties where they're asking the  trainees to perform  medical training that they've done  earlier today in addition to having to  get ready to get on the helicopter  and if you can't get on the helicopter  you don't pass the course good job you  did it  excellent is it more dangerous to be a  diplomat now than it was 20 years ago  to say the world is more challenging i  think that's probably a fair statement  the diplomats of today are not  they're not drinking gin and tonics on  the terrace our military uh  colleagues take on significant risks  overseas but so do our diplomats and  and i'm very pleased that we've now have  this facility to train them as they  should be trained and be prepared for  what comes  successful statecraft requires proper  preparation  better to have the training and not need  it then to need it  and not know what to do for cbs this  morning saturday christina rafini  blackstone virginia  great elements there i've done one of  these courses and it gives you an  appreciation not just for the diplomats  but for the people protecting them  who you don't always see in the  spotlight or at the microphone and what  christina was saying there at the end  and what they  the point is that it's so much better to  have this training should you need it  than if you're sitting there and  suddenly don't know when  we've seen the impact of when you don't  have it  and what it can do

